    "created_at": "2020-05-14T20:59:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-14T21:51:31Z",
    "body": "Seems like vi mode detection is not implemented for Bash\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/starship/starship/blob/879f2ec5da5d38416373e84458af433c754081c2/src/modules/character.rs#L36-L38\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is probably not possible to implement in Starship (unless there's some crazy hack/workaround).\r\n\r\nThe way vi mode can be displayed in prompt for bash is one of these two snippets:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n# ~/.inputrc\r\nset show-mode-in-prompt on\r\nset vi-cmd-mode-string \"[N]\"\r\nset vi-ins-mode-string \"[I]\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nor,\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n# ~/.bashrc\r\nbind 'set show-mode-in-prompt on'\r\nbind 'set vi-cmd-mode-string \"[N]\"'\r\nbind 'set vi-ins-mode-string \"[I]\"'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is handled by [GNU Readline](https://tiswww.case.edu/php/chet/readline/rltop.html)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
